Proposal c4a9acef79bd5295 expected unchanged but executed as unrunnable. The proposer did not misread the rule: the rule as written and the code agree. The rule says 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text', and recover_json_object implements that by iterating `for pool in (fenced, top_level):` and `for candidate in reversed(pool):`. The failure is in the input encoding: the proposal JSON used `\\n` and `\\\"`, which decode to literal backslash-n and backslash-quote, not newlines and quotes. So the fenced content is `\n{\"a\": 1}\n`, which is not valid JSON, and the top-level scan sees `{\"a\": 1}`, also invalid. The code therefore reaches `raise RecordError(\"no JSON object could be recovered from the response\")` and the harness records ' raised'. The proposer should build next a pair with actual newlines and quotes (single-escaped in JSON) to test that the last fenced object wins.